{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795312110,"nonce":"5QHFe227XjszNTG1Ih2QmPnAfjQ=","title":"zrtl_thread: mutex_lock never releases and channel_recv holds a global lock while it waits","message":"Found while annotating the plugin's waits for the Immix collector (61fbc22). Both are older than that work.\n\nmutex_lock takes the lock, forgets the guard, and returns. mutex_unlock does nothing. So the second mutex_lock on the same handle, from any thread, waits for ever. The mutex works once. The thread-local HELD_GUARDS map exists but nothing fills it. A fix keeps the guard per handle and per thread, and makes mutex_unlock drop it.\n\nchannel_recv, channel_recv_timeout and channel_recv_timeout_status wait inside Receiver::recv while they hold the global RECEIVERS lock. Every other channel operation on a receiver, for any channel, waits for that one message. Two threads that each wait on a different channel can deadlock when one needs the other's reply. A fix keeps each receiver in its own Arc\u003cMutex\u003cReceiver\u003e\u003e and holds the map lock only to find it.\n\nNeither changes how the collector sees the plugin. A wait on either lock now runs inside a blocking region, so a collection does not wait for it.\n\nNot annotated: sdl_delay and window_delay sleep outside a blocking region. This Mac has no SDL, so the edit could not be built here. Wrap both in zrtl::heap::blocking where SDL is installed.","files":null}]}